  "details": "On Windows, when \"System Default\" is selected as the microphone input in VRChat, it would be more appropriate for it to use the \"Default Communications Device\" rather than the general \"Default Device\".\n\nOn Windows, microphone devices are explicitly separated into:\n\n- Default Device (general audio)\n\n- Default Communications Device (voice and chat applications)\n\nMany voice-focused applications, such as Discord, use the \"Default Communications Device\" for microphone input. This allows users to separate their general audio device and their voice chat device.\n\nAlternatively, it would be nice to allow users to explicitly choose between:\n\n- System Default\n\n- System Communications Default\n\nThis would preserve compatibility with existing settings while giving users more control.",
